  "body": "Found during the work on issue 1735.\n\n## Problem\n\nA blind slot has two side walls and one end wall. The user picks the three top edges as one U-shaped open run. A pocket-family operation (2D Offset, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive) refuses the selection: \"... is an open run - a 2D Offset cannot end mid-edge ...\".\n\nIssue 1735 made two separate open edges a band that the stock outline closes. One open run with one open side is not covered.\n\n## Wanted\n\n- One U-shaped open run is a region with one open side. The stock outline closes the open side.\n- The extension moves the open side out of the stock along the two end tangents of the run.\n- A run whose region is not clear is refused by name.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe gouge check and the collision check must not change. A pass that cuts a kept part must block the post. Pin that with a test that expects the refusal.\n\n## Done means\n\nA pocket-family operation on a blind slot picked as one open run generates a path from the end wall to the stock edge, with a pinning test and a refusal test.\n\nPart of the work that started with #1735.\n",
